MID_EV13_052_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_052_m01_001: We have received word from the temples about the\nschedule and opponent for our semifinal match.
MID_EV13_052_m01_002: Ribeira Winds defeated Rose Tempest to advance.
MID_EV13_052_m01_003: Which means they are the clan we shall face next.
MID_EV13_052_m01_004: Haah...
MID_EV13_052_m01_005: Is something troubling you, Your Majesty?
MID_EV13_052_m01_006: As I recall, Ribeira Winds is Cai's clan. Are you\nfeeling conflicted about the upcoming bout?
MID_EV13_052_m01_007: Fear not. A youth he may be, but a youth standing\nin my way. I shall not hold back.
MID_EV13_052_m01_008: <NCA>Reminisce.
MID_EV13_052_m01_009: It is strange to think that the boy I struck then has\ncome so far.
MID_EV13_052_m01_010: I never would have imagined that he would be an\nobstacle to our long-held dream.
MID_EV13_052_m01_011: Strange indeed. Your Majesty and the boy seem\nto be drawn together by fate.
MID_EV13_052_m01_012: I mislike that word. It abdicates responsibility.
MID_EV13_052_m01_013: Then let us say "causality" instead. It is a concept\nwith its roots in the ancients.
MID_EV13_052_m01_014: The choices Your Majesty and the boy made on that\nday, and all your actions since, have led here.
MID_EV13_052_m01_015: Had anything gone differently, you might not now\nstand opposed to each other.
MID_EV13_052_m01_016: That which appears to be fate is formed from the\nchain of events linked together by causality.
MID_EV13_052_m01_017: I prefer that. It makes this all easier to swallow.
MID_EV13_052_m01_018: I particularly appreciate that it does not lay the\nfault at others' feet.
MID_EV13_052_m01_019: For I find myself a bit envious of him.
MID_EV13_052_m01_020: Your Majesty?
MID_EV13_052_m01_021: Never mind. It's not like me to brood so. Forget I\nsaid anything.
MID_EV13_052_m01_022: <NCA>Think about Cai.
MID_EV13_052_m01_023: <NCB>Think about the other trouble.
MID_EV13_052_m01_024: <ACA>Still, it takes more than luck for one to advance\nso far through the Heroic Games.
MID_EV13_052_m01_025: <ACA>Thinking back on it, there was always something\nslightly uncanny about him.
MID_EV13_052_m01_026: <ACA>Throughout the tournament, he was matched with\nmany powerful foes. He must have considerable skill.
MID_EV13_052_m01_027: <ACA>Let us not underestimate him. He is no mere boy;\nhe is a true warrior.
MID_EV13_052_m01_028: <ACA>As am I. Which means we shall meet strength\nfor strength.
MID_EV13_052_m01_029: <ACB>There is one more unresolved matter that has been\nhanging over me.
MID_EV13_052_m01_030: <ACB>Prince Dyan's escape from Fort Cottus, I assume?
MID_EV13_052_m01_031: <ACB>Indeed. It is a gamble which will happen first—my\nvictory here, or the culmination of his scheme.
MID_EV13_052_m01_032: <ACB>But I cannot fathom what he hopes to accomplish,\neven outside of prison.
MID_EV13_052_m01_033: <ACB>Whatever the answer, for now I must focus on\nthe battle in front of me.
MID_EV13_106_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_106_m01_001: It's been some time. Thank you for lending me your\nship, Theodora.
MID_EV13_106_m01_002: The captain of the Trafalgar told me what happened\nafter you made landfall at Solomon.
MID_EV13_106_m01_003: They were told to return without you if you didn't\nmake it back to the ship.
MID_EV13_106_m01_004: So I was worried when you were not aboard the\nship's return voyage. Fortunately, all seems well.
MID_EV13_106_m01_005: Yes, thankfully I made it through safely. Ah, before I\nforget: we managed to secure the seedling for you.
MID_EV13_106_m01_006: A seedling from the pepper trees of Solomon? This\nwill more than cover the cost of the voyage.
MID_EV13_106_m01_007: Thank you, Anatolia. I will see that you are rewarded\nsuitably for this.
MID_EV13_106_m01_008: That is kind of you.
MID_EV13_106_m01_009: Is something the matter?
MID_EV13_106_m01_010: Master Long is dead. He gave his life to protect me.
MID_EV13_106_m01_011: What?! Long is dead? That is unfortunate. I owed\nhim a great deal.
MID_EV13_106_m01_012: I will never have the chance to thank him properly.\nThough this must be harder on you.
MID_EV13_106_m01_013: It was the result of my own pride. I put everyone\nin danger.
MID_EV13_106_m01_014: But Master Long... He laid down his life to clear\nthe way for me despite that. Despite everything.
MID_EV13_106_m01_015: I sympathize with him. I want to build a future for\nSaramis, even if my body is the foundation.
MID_EV13_106_m01_016: I view it as my primary duty as queen.
MID_EV13_106_m01_017: In the same way, Long knew the value of keeping\nyou alive, even at the cost of himself.
MID_EV13_106_m01_018: I would consider myself blessed to have someone\nto carry out my will.
MID_EV13_106_m01_019: And that is what you must now do for Long. It will\nbe hard going, but you are equal to it.
MID_EV13_106_m01_020: Thank you, Theodora.
MID_EV13_071_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_071_m01_001: Ooogh...
MID_EV13_071_m01_002: You! So you've come to haunt me!
MID_EV13_071_m01_003: Do you not want to win this fight? Let loose the\nstrength I offer.
MID_EV13_071_m01_004: Are you or are you not a warrior? Then give yourself\nover to the power.
MID_EV13_071_m01_005: All you must do is sever that chain. Then you will\nunderstand true might.
MID_EV13_071_m01_006: <NCA>Clutch the chain.
MID_EV13_071_m01_007: Rrrhh...
MID_EV13_071_m01_008: You are not Bahr Vahn. He was an evil man,\nbut not like this.
MID_EV13_071_m01_009: What is the matter? Do you not crave power? What\nhave you to fear?
MID_EV13_071_m01_010: It is true that Bahr Vahn was all too willing to\nbecome a demon god.
MID_EV13_071_m01_011: But I am not like him. I will not trade my humanity\nso cheaply.
MID_EV13_071_m01_012: I shall resist for as long as I have a will to do so.
MID_EV13_071_m01_013: Begone, ghost, and tempt me no more with your\nhoneyed words!
MID_EV13_071_m01_014: Fool!
MID_EV13_071_m01_015: I will use the arm gladly and freely. That is the\nextent of the help I require from you.
MID_EV13_071_m01_016: Boss? Psst, boss! You can't go spacing out now!
MID_EV13_071_m01_017: Um, Theodora...are you OK?
MID_EV13_071_m01_018: Yes. Pardon me. I will collect myself.
MID_EV13_071_m01_019: Bonaventure, how long was my episode?
MID_EV13_071_m01_020: Roughly the count of 10, give or take.
MID_EV13_071_m01_021: I see. So he stopped attacking for a time and waited\nhonorably, did he?
MID_EV13_071_m01_022: Had he exploited my dazed state, he could have\nclaimed victory in an instant.
MID_EV13_071_m01_023: You are noble to the point of foolishness. I respect it.
MID_EV13_071_m01_024: Huh? Were you—were you talking to me?
MID_EV13_071_m01_025: Never mind. I was singing your praises, but the\nmoment has passed.
MID_EV13_071_m01_026: Now we are again at war. Come! Let us finish this!
MID_EV13_055_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_055_m01_001: If Cai collapsed after the match, he must have found\nthe limits of his strength.
MID_EV13_055_m01_002: I hoped to see proof that he is alright, but he may\nnot wish to see me...
MID_EV13_055_m01_003: Perhaps I should come back another time.
MID_EV13_055_m01_004: Queen Theodora? Did you...want to come in?
MID_EV13_055_m01_005: Hmmmmmm?
MID_EV13_055_m01_006: <NCA>Avert your eyes.
MID_EV13_055_m01_007: I...merely happened to be passing. Do not assume\nI was worried about Cai.
MID_EV13_055_m01_008: Queen Theodora, do you think you could talk to Cai\nfor me?
MID_EV13_055_m01_009: Er, I suppose. Is he fit for conversation? If so, I shall\nput in an appearance.
MID_EV13_055_m01_010: Is he...awake?
MID_EV13_055_m01_011: Cai? Queen Theodora is here to see you.
MID_EV13_055_m01_012: Theodora...you're so strong. Too strong for me, huh?
MID_EV13_055_m01_013: Hello, Cai.
MID_EV13_055_m01_014: On the bright side, I'd say I made it pretty far.
MID_EV13_055_m01_015: I thought I was doing so good, and then... Something\nabout you changed partway through, didn't it?
MID_EV13_055_m01_016: Perhaps. But don't be too proud of yourself for\nthinking you had the better of me.
MID_EV13_055_m01_017: Yeah, I guess you're right. It's still frustrating though.
MID_EV13_055_m01_018: Indulge my curiosity, Cai. What boon would you\nhave wished for?
MID_EV13_055_m01_019: My dad's in prison. Unless something changes,\nthey're going to execute him.
MID_EV13_055_m01_020: So I wanted to win the Heroic Games and ask\nLord Solel to pardon my dad.
MID_EV13_055_m01_021: I see. I had no inkling of this. I...I am sorry.
MID_EV13_055_m01_022: It's fine. It was a long shot anyway.
MID_EV13_055_m01_023: I was just so desperate...but I guess you are too, with\nyour own wish.
MID_EV13_055_m01_024: It comes down to who wins and who loses. There's\nno way around that.
MID_EV13_055_m01_025: But I'm still going to save Pop. There has to be\na way.
MID_EV13_055_m01_026: That is laudably optimistic of you.
MID_EV13_055_m01_027: Now that I'm out, I hope you do what I couldn't,\nTheodora.
MID_EV13_055_m01_028: Keep the dream alive, OK? I'll be cheering for you.
MID_EV13_055_m01_029: I will fight with all I have.
MID_EV13_055_m01_030: {SetColor=Gray}Because unlike you, I cannot yet afford the luxury\nof optimism.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_056_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_056_m01_001: Your Majesty! I have an urgent matter you must\nhear. I warn you, it's bad.
MID_EV13_056_m01_002: Again? What now?
MID_EV13_056_m01_003: Details are sparse, since the first messenger was\ndispatched as soon as possible.
MID_EV13_056_m01_004: But the Mosa have launched an all-out assault on\nthe new region of Ogmios. Fort Zanbar has fallen.
MID_EV13_056_m01_005: What?! That fortress is not taken easily.
MID_EV13_056_m01_006: Based on what we know so far...they had some sort\nof inside help.
MID_EV13_056_m01_007: Once they let the Mosa infiltrators in, the gates were\nthrown open and their army pushed through.
MID_EV13_056_m01_008: <NCA>Ask for details.
MID_EV13_056_m01_009: <NCB>Ask about Dyan.
MID_EV13_056_m01_010: <ACA>How can this be? And at the worst possible time.
MID_EV13_056_m01_011: <ACA>There are several other things that concern me about\nwhat we know so far.
MID_EV13_056_m01_012: <ACA>First, this is not their usual approach. The Mosa\ntend to use simple, direct tactics.
MID_EV13_056_m01_013: <ACA>Yet this time they knew to strike at Fort Zanbar\nwhere it was weakest.
MID_EV13_056_m01_014: <ACA>The soldiers present confirmed that some among the\nMosa forces appeared to be Saraminians.
MID_EV13_056_m01_015: <ACA>Put more plainly, we have a traitor.
MID_EV13_056_m01_016: <ACA>Precisely. All signs suggest that someone from\nSaramis is colluding with the Mosa.
MID_EV13_056_m01_017: <ACB>Could this be Dyan's faction at work in a bid to\ntake Saramis by force?
MID_EV13_056_m01_018: <ACB>Quite possible, but it requires believing that a royal\nscion would sell out their own country.
MID_EV13_056_m01_019: <ACB>A cornered rat will do anything. The fact that they\nknow our internal affairs is troubling.
MID_EV13_056_m01_020: <ACB>Um...just so you know, I've never actually been\ncontacted by or worked with the Dyan faction.
MID_EV13_056_m01_021: <ACB>Though if I'm honest, I'd love a chance to check in\nwith my folks real quick.
MID_EV13_056_m01_022: <ACB>Worry not. I do not doubt your loyalties.
MID_EV13_056_m01_023: Another report states that the Mosa have occupied\nFort Zanbar and are fortifying their defenses.
MID_EV13_056_m01_024: We must act swiftly. What are your orders,\nYour Majesty?
MID_EV13_056_m01_025: For the Mosa to hold that position is for them to have\na blade to our throat.
MID_EV13_056_m01_026: We can still stand fast at Grania Stronghold, but it\ncannot endure forever.
MID_EV13_056_m01_027: If the situation worsens in my absence, it may spiral\nout of all possible control.
MID_EV13_056_m01_028: Victory at the Heroic Games is almost mine for\nthe taking.
MID_EV13_056_m01_029: But we cannot afford to neglect Megaira any longer.
MID_EV13_056_m01_030: Just so. Should Megaira fall, the Mosa incursion\nwould no doubt continue north into this land.
MID_EV13_056_m01_031: I ask again, Your Majesty. What are your orders?
MID_EV13_056_m01_032: <NCA>Make your decision.
MID_EV13_056_m01_033: We will withdraw from the Heroic Games and set\nsail tomorrow for Megaira.
MID_EV13_056_m01_034: Notify the soldiers that we are leaving. Prepare the\nTrafalgar for departure at once.
MID_EV13_056_m01_035: A wise decision. The people will understand how\ndeeply Your Majesty regrets this.
MID_EV13_056_m01_036: Should we inform Lord Solel?
MID_EV13_056_m01_037: The Divine Sovereign has sharp ears. We should\nassume he will learn of this soon.
MID_EV13_056_m01_038: I would have him learn it from me rather than\nbelieve I am sweeping it under the rug.
MID_EV13_056_m01_039: However, there is a loose end I wish to address in\nDagsion first.
MID_EV13_067_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_067_m01_001: Your Majesty, you're safe! What a relief this is.
MID_EV13_067_m01_002: So how'd it go, boss? Didja get to meet Aurora?
MID_EV13_067_m01_003: Yes. She was even more wonderful than I imagined.
MID_EV13_067_m01_004: Our time in Dagsion was worth it if only to have\nmet her.
MID_EV13_067_m01_005: You would have called her a "maiden," Bonaventure.\nAnd something of her felt similar to the cat priest.
MID_EV13_067_m01_006: Oh? Most interesting. Would that I could have had\nmy own audience with her.
MID_EV13_067_m01_007: <NCA>Reminisce.
MID_EV13_067_m01_008: Had it not been for the boy's interference so long ago,\nour meeting may never have come to pass.
MID_EV13_067_m01_009: Happenstance brought me to him. Should this, too,\nbe chalked up to causality?
MID_EV13_067_m01_010: Something seems different with you, boss. Like you\ngot rid of some evil spirit haunting you.
MID_EV13_067_m01_011: No doubt due to Aurora locking away this arm's\nmalice for me.
MID_EV13_067_m01_012: Until now, I was resolute in believing my only role\nwas to fulfill Saramis's long-held dream.
MID_EV13_067_m01_013: With seven years left to live, I assumed my life\nwould be forfeit to this goal.
MID_EV13_067_m01_014: But now...I feel that Aurora's love washing over me\nhas caused a change in my thinking.
MID_EV13_067_m01_015: Intriguing. How do you mean?
MID_EV13_067_m01_016: I haven't the precise words for it. Hope, perhaps.\nI want to live to see the fruition of Saramis's dream.
MID_EV13_067_m01_017: But it's more than that. I'm coming around to the\nidea of being a mother.
MID_EV13_067_m01_018: Oh, happy day! I thought I might never hear those\nwords from Your Majesty's lips!
MID_EV13_067_m01_019: This is good, right? We all think this is good? Well,\nthe boss is smiling, so that's enough for me.
MID_EV13_067_m01_020: If you're getting attached to the idea of living,\nI'm all for it.
MID_EV13_067_m01_021: My only fear is that I may have sacrificed some\npower in exchange.
MID_EV13_067_m01_022: So what? Me and Bona would be there for you,\nboss. That's what right and left arms are for.
MID_EV13_067_m01_023: Lil and Sander feel the same. Not to mention the\nrank-and-file troops.
MID_EV13_067_m01_024: Thank you. All of you.
MID_EV13_067_m01_025: Bonaventure...hypothetically speaking...
MID_EV13_067_m01_026: What would you think of a husband closer to my\nown age than our previous candidates?
MID_EV13_067_m01_027: P-pardon, Your Majesty?
MID_EV13_067_m01_028: Would a younger man not suit me? I wonder what\nthe people of Saramis would think.
MID_EV13_067_m01_029: No, no, no, no, no. There is nothing wrong with it!\nI do see the merit in the idea.
MID_EV13_067_m01_030: Once we are home, I shall select the best from the\nyounger candidates we had not yet considered.
MID_EV13_067_m01_031: And after this Mosa uprising is put down, I shall\nmake arrangements for Your Majesty to meet them.
MID_EV13_067_m01_032: I will not rest until we produce a partner to your\nliking. You shall have many options to choose from!
MID_EV13_067_m01_033: Put your faith in the discerning eye of your humble\nservant Bonaventure!
MID_EV13_067_m01_034: I will find someone who meets Your Majesty's\nstandards and introduce the two of you at once!
MID_EV13_067_m01_035: Wow, look at Bona go! I ain't seen him this fired up\nin a long, long time.
MID_EV13_067_m01_036: That is enough, you two. Let us not get carried away.